COMPILATION OF: E49I3

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49I3

   1 a 0000 E49I3:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P4] `rec.s2 > rec.na' -- the INVERSION PAIR of E49F2:
   4 a 0006      same relation `>', extents swapped in writing.  `> ' is
   5 a 0006      lowered SWAPPED, so na loads first: `06 03 / 3E 02', JNC d2.
   6 a 0006      This row re-tests whether lengths follow the lowered operands
   7 a 0006      in the OTHER unequal orientation (F2 measured one direction of
   8 a 0006      the swap only). */
   9 c 0006   dcl
  10 c 0006     1 rec,
  11 c 0006       2 na char(3),
  12 c 0006       2 nb char(3),
  13 c 0006       2 s2 char(2);
  14 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  15 c 0006   if rec.s2 > rec.na then k = 1;
  16 c 001E   put list('K=', k);
  17 c 0040   stop;
  18 a 0043 end E49I3;

CODE SIZE = 0043
DATA AREA = 000C
FREE SYMS = 3888
END  COMPILATION
